This is an UNOFFICIAL extension. It is not made, endorsed or supported by
Overleaf, and "Overleaf" is used only to say which site it works with.

Third-party material:

- PhiTeX (phitex-ssa, phitex-layout, phitex-syntax, phitex-tex), linked
  into core.wasm: MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- core/tex/plain.tex and core/tex/hyphen.tex (TeX Live's, unmodified), built
  into core.wasm: plain TeX by Donald E. Knuth, and Knuth's hyphenation
  patterns; distributed unchanged, as their terms ask.
- core/fonts/*.tfm: the Computer Modern font metrics (Knuth; the copies
  PhiTeX carries), unmodified, built into core.wasm.
- extension/src/panel.ts: approximateFraction, ported from pdf.js
  (pdfjs-dist 5.1.91, web/pdf_viewer.mjs), Copyright Mozilla Foundation,
  Apache-2.0.
- extension/src/panel.ts: icon paths from Google's Material Icons,
  Apache-2.0.
- The toolbar and popover markup the extension adds to Overleaf's page
  follows Overleaf's own (overleaf/overleaf, services/web/frontend),
  AGPL-3.0.

texmf/ (shipped as extension/texmf/): LaTeX packages from TeX Live 2026
(the LaTeX kernel and classes, l3kernel, graphics, tools, amsmath, hyperref,
...; texmf/MANIFEST.tsv lists each package and revision), unmodified, each
under its own license as stated in its files, mostly the LaTeX Project
Public License 1.3c. Packages not bundled are downloaded as needed from
Shelf (shelf-phitex.pages.dev), which serves TeX Live's files unmodified.
